        "noteCount": 7,
        "notes": [
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_0",
            "severity": "info",
            "category": "opening",
            "message": "The opening hook regarding the 'lying' lamp is masterful and immediately establishes the magic system's texture."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_1",
            "severity": "suggest",
            "category": "pacing",
            "message": "The transition to the Commission Hall feels slightly abrupt; consider a brief sentence to bridge the silence of the shop with the bustle of the Hall."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_2",
            "severity": "info",
            "category": "characterization",
            "message": "The 'Company' feels distinct and lived-in, especially through Brick's quiet, observant gesture with the apple."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_3",
            "severity": "suggest",
            "category": "show-don't-tell",
            "message": "The line 'Cael tried not to read anything into and read everything into anyway' is a bit cliché; trust the subtext of the interaction instead."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_4",
            "severity": "flag",
            "category": "POV",
            "message": "The internal monologue during the walk home, 'Because you and not us are the same...', feels slightly too expository for Cael's guarded character."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_5",
            "severity": "info",
            "category": "voice",
            "message": "The prose is exceptionally rhythmic, particularly the description of the lamp's flicker 'like a person trying to remember a name'."
          },
          {
            "id": "note_mrvje0r8_6",
            "severity": "suggest",
            "category": "tension",
            "message": "The connection between the lamp's 'note' and the token's 'hum' is excellent, but ensure the physical sensation for Cael is even more visceral to heighten the stakes."
          }
        ],
